From 9289e55cbc80cea6fd506792c73fb5b1e2209342 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ewan McIntyre <ewan3568@me.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 15:58:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] Trip builder: free to send, Where to? search, best order,
 stages + log in, Ask Ewan, security, accessibility

A sync of public/trip-builder from the builder repo (node scripts/sync-allin.mjs).

Free to send:
- Sending a trip costs nothing. The form says so, the trip page and the "choose how to pay" screen no longer talk about a
  deposit for a trip that didn't take one, and the page follows what the backend answers (a payment link in the reply means
  "go and pay it first"). Needs backend patch 0007 and DEPOSIT_PER_PERSON: 0 in config.js (patch 0007 sets it).
- Paying after approval: all now, a week before they leave (a card is saved first, nothing charged) or instalments.

Easier to use:
- "Where to?" on the home page and in the builder: type a hostel, country, tour, ALL IN trip or classic route
  (typos forgiven), pick it, and it starts a trip or adds it where it adds the least travel (after where you land on a tie).
- Best order: puts the stops in the order that costs the least travel; Undo takes it back.
- A quiz you can leave after the landing point ("Skip the rest and show my routes").

Plan in stages, and log in:
- After sending a trip: "Plan my next stage". The builder carries on from where the guest is, shows where they have
  been, and never suggests a place they have been to again. Sent as stage 2, 3, ... (needs backend patch 0005).
- "Log in with your email" on the home page emails a link to each trip they sent. No password
  (needs the new trip-builder-login function from patch 0005).

A real person checks every trip:
- "Plan it here. A real human checks it before anything is booked." and an Ask Ewan button (WhatsApp, with the trip
  already in the message) on every screen.

Safer:
- Content-Security-Policy, no inline handlers, everything a guest typed is escaped, links only if http(s).
- "Forget my trip and details on this device" for shared computers.
- A trip page no longer redraws over the screen the guest has moved on to.

Accessibility and phones: axe-core clean on every screen and modal; labelled, trapped and returned focus in modals;
a route announcer, a skip link, one h1 per screen; the 320px header and hero fixed; 44px tap targets on touch.

Speed: small WebP copies of the photos where PHOTO_BASE or THUMB_BASE is set. The live copy hot-links the full photos, so
it gets the small ones with `node scripts/sync-allin.mjs <site> --with-thumbs` (optional, not in this patch).
Exchange rates updated to 22 Oct 2026.

